Below is the exact HTTP request you can send to VirusTotal to retrieve the **sub‑domain** relationships for `example.org`.  
It limits the results to 10 items, uses the continuation cursor `abc`, and asks the API to return only the `id` and `context_attributes` fields for each related object.

```
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related
    ?relationship=subdomains
    &limit=10
    &continuation_cursor=abc
    &fields=id,context_attributes

Headers:
    x-apikey: my_api
```

**What you’ll receive**

The JSON response will look something like this (truncated for brevity):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "context_attributes": { ... }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "context_attributes": { ... }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "links": { ... },
  "meta": { ... }
}
```

Only the `id` and `context_attributes` of each related object are returned, as requested.  

If you need to paginate further, use the `continuation_cursor` value from the `meta` section of the response.
